e clearing 2.6% requires the >=+0.50pp TFP branch that 2B itself prices at only 23%\"). That is using the ensemble's own prior as evidence about the world - circular, and it is scope insensitivity on the upside: 2.6% coupled growth does NOT require a TFP breakout, it requires China at 3.5% and the OECD at 1.8%, both of which have five-year precedent inside the last decade. P10 = 0.90 (one synchronized recession plus China at ~1.5%), P50 = 2.25, P90 = 3.40. Implied left sigma 1.05, right sigma 0.90 - wider on both sides than any Wave-1 panelist, which is the correct red-team shape when the centre was built by stacking point adjustments.","referenceClassIds":[],"schemaVersion":"forecast-workbench.forecast/v1","sealedAt":"2026-11-04T17:31:58.336Z","seriesId":"published-panel","strongestContraryCase":"Not elicited per question. Panelist falsification signposts: {\"signpost\":\"FRED DFII10 twelve-month trailing average >= 2.75% AND the NY Fed ACM 10-year nominal term premium >= 1.50%, with no new Fed purchase programme, Treasury buyback expansion, SLR recalibration or statutory captive-demand mandate announced in the interim.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2028\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Directly falsifies both my low term premium (+0.55) and my 0.60 repression probability. CQ4 P50 moves up 55-70bp to ~1.75 and the whole distribution loses its left skew; CQ6-C rises ~6pp to ~18 and CQ6-A falls ~6pp to ~27; CQ5 rises from 15 to ~26 via the MOVE conjunct. This is the Wave-1 central case being right and me being wrong for the reason they would name.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"An MSCI World peak-to-trough drawdown of >= 25% occurs AND G7 GDP-weighted 10-year nominal sovereign yields rise >= 25bp (or fail to fall 50bp) through the drawdown window.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2031\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies my core CQ5 claim that a capex-bust drawdown is disinflationary and bond-bullish; my P(no rally | drawdown) of 0.28 would be revealed as the wrong template. CQ5 resolves on the 